<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Rain seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Rain seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   25.6</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    30</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  14.2</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 18.2</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     14.9</p>
<p>    Norton		   10.1</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    1.5</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   4</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department said occasional thundershowers will be experienced over the Central, Sabaragamuwa, Western and Southern provinces and over the sea area off west and south coasts, on Thursday. There will also be fairely strong southwesterly winds along the western slopes of the central hills, the department said.</p>
